  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "76972484-f773-40c8-99cc-7d9e8cb39ec6",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 864,
        "content": "## Contract Price Compliance Checker (Google Sheets + Telegram)\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow monitors a Google Sheets invoice sheet for newly added rows, retrieves the relevant contract pricing data, and compares the invoice price against the contracted price. It logs each comparison to an overcharge report, then branches based on whether an overcharge or missing contract price was detected. If a problem is found, it sends a Telegram alert; otherwise, it ends without further action.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials for both the invoice trigger sheet, the contract prices sheet, and the overcharge report sheet.\n- Configure the Google Sheets trigger to watch the correct invoice spreadsheet and worksheet for new rows.\n- Set the contract price lookup node to read from the correct contract pricing spreadsheet or range.\n- Review the comparison code so it matches invoice items to contract prices using the correct column names and price rules.\n- Connect Telegram credentials and configure the destination chat ID for overcharge alerts.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the comparison logic for tolerances, currency handling, item matching rules, or additional alert conditions such as missing vendors or unusually high quantities."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
